#: ../../source/docs/brake-mode.rst:5
#: 7c36291555814e668920dbbd57837762
msgid "Brake Mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/brake-mode.rst:7
#: 2148597b9b814e60887ac35c507e09d1
msgid "This very simple flight mode simply stops the vehicle as soon as possible.  Once invoked, this mode does not accept any input from the pilot. This mode requires a valid position estimate."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/brake-mode.rst:11
#: d8e3bd7cbcc04d58949253d58832af8c
msgid "Brake mode is subject to acceleration and angle limits imposed by the position and attitude controllers. For more aggressive braking, you can also try increasing :ref:`PSC_JERK_NE <PSC_JERK_NE>`. As an example use case, a value of 15 to 30 works well for a small copter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/brake-mode.rst:17
#: 41554bff2ad545e7bcb8f48274b65f17
msgid "Overview"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/brake-mode.rst:19
#: 0e33dd41caec47389f696f6cc6828b02
msgid "When switched on, Brake mode will attempt to stop the vehicle as quickly as possible.  Good GPS position, :ref:`low magnetic interference on the compass <common-diagnosing-problems-using-logs_compass_interference>`\\ and :ref:`low vibrations <common-diagnosing-problems-using-logs_vibrations>` are all important in achieving good performance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/brake-mode.rst:30
#: 0f95bf2b454f4ccba4524ad989535748
msgid "Controls"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/brake-mode.rst:32
#: e2b06e2b5fda49ad851fcf7665381fbc
msgid "The pilots controls are ignored in this mode.  The vehicle must be switched out of this mode before the pilot can re-take control."
msgstr ""
